WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.400
Hey guys,
Welcome back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:08.520
the second part of the series, where we talk about&nbsp;
biblical financial principles every man must know.&nbsp;

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.060
In a previous video, we talked&nbsp;
about never creating debt.&nbsp;

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.320
Never spending money you don't&nbsp;
have on things you don't need.&nbsp;

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.220
Then we talked about investing.
And then we talked about creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.580
a budget every month.
Now, we're going to talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.420
about a total of eight things when it&nbsp;
comes to biblical financial principles.&nbsp;

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:35.520
And number five is saving money.
Specifically, saving money for the unknown future.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.020
[Proverbs 21:20]

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.620
It is very important to save money&nbsp;
for the future because you never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.400
know what the future will hold, right?
But also it is important to save money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.400 --> 00:01:00.300
for anything - unexpectedly - that can happen&nbsp;
at any time and then you're not ready for it.&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.980
You can do this by just putting aside&nbsp;
a portion of your income each month&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:12.600
into a savings account or an emergency fund.
Look, you never expect a flat tire but it happens.&nbsp;

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:18.960
In the same way you never expect your&nbsp;
water heater to burst, but it happens.&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.940
And those who do not plan for the&nbsp;
future, they're just planning to fail.&nbsp;

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.880
Unexpected things will happen.
And if you're not ready for it - your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:34.800
whole family - you - you'll be in trouble.
So, all you got to do is save your money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:41.040
for those, let's call it those flat tire days.
So that when it happens, you know you have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:46.260
money tucked away and it will solve the problem.
And then you will still have bread on the table.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:47.580
[Proverbs 21:20]

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.900
You know, there are always&nbsp;
those who are gluttonous.&nbsp;

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.020
They are greedy for money.
And when they have money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:10.020
they just want to spend it.
They just want to live for the now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.200
instead of thinking for the future.
Preparing for the future.&nbsp;

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.380
There are many people out&nbsp;
there who think like this...&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.620
Man, I still have one hundred dollars left.
Hmmm. What am I going to spend this on?&nbsp;

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:26.280
Instead of thinking man, I still&nbsp;
have one hundred dollars left,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:34.200
let me save this for the future in case I need it.
Those who spend it recklessly find themselves in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:40.440
need of money time and time again and they even&nbsp;
get angry when people do not want to help them.&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.080
Even when they ask their family.&nbsp;

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:47.220
If you have a family member or a friend&nbsp;
like this, then you should not help them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.400
because you're actually helping them to stay&nbsp;
in that position and never learn their lesson.&nbsp;

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:55.860
They're thinking, man, I have money.
I'm just going to spend it.&nbsp;

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.980
And then when I come to that point where&nbsp;
they don't have money, oh I'm gonna ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.020
John, I'm gonna ask Susan.
They will always help me.&nbsp;

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:05.400
And then I keep on doing that.
They stay in that comfort zone.&nbsp;

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.700
You will help them more if&nbsp;
you don't give them money.&nbsp;

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.180
Because then they will learn.
Man, it's my own actions that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:15.780
brought me into this position.
Now I'm in trouble so I'm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:19.140
not going to do this again.
We have an Afrikaans saying...

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.380
If this is you and you just spend money without&nbsp;
thinking about it, then you need to know that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:36.480
there's always consequences.
You will reap what you sow.&nbsp;

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:41.940
If you sow not thinking, just spending all the&nbsp;
time, what do you think is going to happen?&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:47.700
You're going to have trouble.
You will reap what you sow.&nbsp;

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:52.080
But there's good news.
The good news is that you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.700
change and that you can change today.
Let's move on to the next one.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.040
Avoid get rich quick schemes.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:05.940
[Proverbs 13:11]

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:21.960
God's blessing will be upon you if you&nbsp;
work hard for the bread on the table.&nbsp;

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.600
For your money.
If you walk within His will, what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:31.080
He wants you to do, but not if you want to join&nbsp;
get rich quick schemes and do you want to just try&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:37.320
some shortcuts to get ahead - even bribing people&nbsp;
in business - His blessing will not be upon you.&nbsp;

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:44.580
Also, if you do the lottery or you&nbsp;
go gambling, Isaiah 65:11-12 says...

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:24.000
Trying to get rich quick often leads to financial&nbsp;
ruin because you're doing that ... you're walking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.280
in your own will.
Your own desire.&nbsp;

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.280
Fleshly desires.
You're not walking in God's will.&nbsp;

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:34.440
We need to work hard for&nbsp;
the money that we receive.&nbsp;

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.540
You need to earn it and then you can&nbsp;
focus on making wise financial decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:45.180
over time, like investing in stable&nbsp;
long-term investment opportunities.&nbsp;

00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:51.240
If you work hard for your money, if you walk&nbsp;
within God's will and do what He wants you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:56.640
to do with your life, He will bless you.
You don't want to make the wrong decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:03.660
and not have God's blessing on your life.&nbsp;
That's the worst thing that can happen to you.

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:12.960
Choose your friends wisely.
Now, you might think Daniel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:17.520
what does this have to do with&nbsp;
biblical financial principles?&nbsp;

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:22.260
Well, everything.
Dave Ramsey also talks about it.&nbsp;

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:26.640
He's very wise and also well known talking&nbsp;
about biblical financial principles.&nbsp;

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.840
And I watched some of his videos,&nbsp;
especially when I was younger.&nbsp;

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:34.620
And it's interesting just to&nbsp;
hear what he says about this.&nbsp;

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:41.040
But your friends will influence you and&nbsp;
that includes the way you handle your money.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:43.140
[Proverbs 27:17]

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:51.900
[1 Corinthians 15:33]

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:59.280
Do not be deceived.
Bad company ruins good morals.&nbsp;

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:03.240
You see, children learn the&nbsp;
habits of their parents.&nbsp;

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:06.600
They start to mimic you, and you -&nbsp;
when you look - you just say, oh man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.600 --> 00:07:11.520
he's doing the same thing that I've been doing.
And I didn't even notice that he learned this.&nbsp;

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:15.540
I didn't even teach it to him because&nbsp;
they watch you carefully and it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.020
the same thing when they go to school.
They pick up things from their friends.&nbsp;

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:23.940
Wrong habits at times when they come home and&nbsp;
you realize, man, this is something different.&nbsp;

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.920
I didn't teach.
Where did you learn this?&nbsp;

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:29.940
And you start that conversation and&nbsp;
when we grow up nothing changes.&nbsp;

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:33.000
Truth is truth, right?
So it doesn't change.&nbsp;

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.660
We still pick up things from&nbsp;
the people we mingle with.&nbsp;

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:43.920
From our friends, especially who you spend most of&nbsp;
your time with, and this truth will never change.&nbsp;

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:49.200
Bad friends will make you worse and&nbsp;
good friends will make you better.&nbsp;

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:54.060
Inspiring you to improve yourself.
If you hang around with friends who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:59.280
make good business decisions - who plan&nbsp;
ahead and who educate themselves with good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.820
books - you will learn from them.
And want to do the same.&nbsp;

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:08.820
And this will influence the way you handle money.
Let's move on to the next one, and the last one.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:21.300
Trust in and honor God with your finances.
Ultimately, our financial security and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.740
our ultimate well-being comes&nbsp;
from God in the first place.&nbsp;

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:32.100
And it continues that way especially for us as&nbsp;
reborn Christians as we grow spiritually in Him.&nbsp;

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:38.220
Everything we do, we do through the Spirit.
And that includes the way you handle your money.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:39.060
[Proverbs 3:5]

00:08:54.780 --> 00:09:00.180
By trusting God and following&nbsp;
His principles, that is how you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:06.960
can have true financial peace and security.
And you will be a better businessman with God.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.780
Proverbs 3 verse 9-10 says...

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:29.400
Let me ask you a question.
Do you honor God with your money?&nbsp;

00:09:30.600 --> 00:09:36.600
In this temporary world, you should&nbsp;
use your finances to honor God.&nbsp;

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:41.580
And use it to further His kingdom.
Because when you die and you stand before Him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.380
what will He say to you?
What have you done with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:51.240
the money that I've given you?
You see, by giving generously you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:58.500
can take part in God's work while you are still&nbsp;
here on this earth and also enjoy His blessings.

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:00.960
[2 Corinthians 9:6-7]

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:19.440
meaning the Holy Spirit needs to lead you.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:34.920
I can tell you this with confidence - if&nbsp;
you prove that you can be trusted with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:40.080
money then God might bless you more&nbsp;
financially because He knows He can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:45.900
trust you to use it responsibly and make&nbsp;
wise decisions to use it for His kingdom.&nbsp;

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:51.180
Or do you think God will just bless you with&nbsp;
money to spend it on your own fleshly desires?&nbsp;

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:55.320
That you want to live in luxury for&nbsp;
just this short temporary world?&nbsp;

00:10:55.320 --> 00:11:00.960
To live in pleasure only for yourself?
And you know this is exactly why He does not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.960 --> 00:11:05.520
bless certain people with money when they ask Him.
Because He knows this is what they will do.

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:07.020
[James 4:3]

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:25.140
So God will bless you&nbsp;
financially if it is His will.&nbsp;

00:11:25.140 --> 00:11:29.280
And if He knows that He can trust you.
And first, when He does bless you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:34.080
you need to have financial security yourself&nbsp;
first before you can help other people.

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:35.640
[Proverbs 14:21]

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:46.680
So you need to help the poor but you need&nbsp;
to be wise in how you do that because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:54.180
the old saying of if you just buy a poor man&nbsp;
a fish, he'll expect you to do that always.&nbsp;

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:59.460
But if you buy him the equipment to catch&nbsp;
fish himself, you'll feed him forever, right?&nbsp;

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:06.300
Not only do you need to help the poor,&nbsp;
you also need to help the kingdom of God.&nbsp;

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:09.000
What does that mean?
You can support&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:15.660
preachers - missionaries - and also ministries.
Even online ministries like DLM.&nbsp;

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:20.280
People who rely on God to send&nbsp;
them the money, to share the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:27.600
Gospel the way that He wants them to do it.
And God usually does that through his children.&nbsp;

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:33.600
Brothers and sisters in Christ, that He blesses&nbsp;
financially and expects them to help those who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.380
do not have normal work hours.
You know, just Monday to Friday.&nbsp;

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:42.120
But all that they do is sharing the gospel.
That is their full-time jobs.&nbsp;

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:46.860
You know, when Israel did not&nbsp;
give back to God, He warned them.

00:12:46.860 --> 00:12:49.320
God says in Malachi 3 verse 8:

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:30.480
And let me read this verse to&nbsp;
you again in the New Testament.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:32.580
[2 Corinthians 9:6-7]

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:56.580
[2 Corinthians 9:12]

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:14.280
You know, I just want to say this.
Whatever church you are going to,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:20.040
I grew up in a church.
I saw my dad working day and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:23.880
night - people knocking - people phoning - and&nbsp;
then he has to preach in the sermons and after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:29.040
the sermons work with people - psychological&nbsp;
stuff - help them to grow spiritually - and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:33.480
they were things at their homes.
I mean, the whole week, day and night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:40.680
and I saw how much it costs to run&nbsp;
a church, to do all these things.&nbsp;

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:47.040
To put on the lights and then still people&nbsp;
complained about giving money to the church.&nbsp;

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:51.480
After all that work.
And listen carefully - you should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:55.980
not give money to fake churches.
To churches of false teachers.&nbsp;

00:14:56.640 --> 00:15:02.040
But you should help the true&nbsp;
church of God to do its work.&nbsp;

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:07.140
To save souls and to help people&nbsp;
grow spiritually in Christ.&nbsp;

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:12.180
You know, this is how the devil works.
People never complain about giving money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:16.920
out when they go to see a movie or when they&nbsp;
go to see a show, you know, or a concert.&nbsp;

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:19.140
Yeah sure, here we go.
Let's go.&nbsp;

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.120
But they expect to go to the church&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:26.100
to get everything for free.
Life-changing sermons through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:30.480
the power of the Holy Spirit.
And they are selfish.&nbsp;

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:34.740
They don't want to give anything to God.
Why?&nbsp;

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:40.740
That is your sinful fleshly heart.
Paul actually talked about this directly.

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.300
[1 Corinthians 9:3]

00:15:48.780 --> 00:15:51.840
You see, this is not something&nbsp;
that just is happening right now.&nbsp;

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:57.240
This is something that was always there,&nbsp;
because humans, we always have our sinful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:03.660
flesh even as Christians and money is one of&nbsp;
the things that brings most of the trouble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.160
Christians experience, even in marriages.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.600
[1 Corinthians 9:4-10]&nbsp;

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:15.180
Now he's been working towards the point&nbsp;
that he wants to make and here it comes.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:46.440
[1 Corinthians 9:11-13]

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:00.180
Now, listen to this.

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:07.500
[1 Corinthians 9:14]

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:17.880
Do you understand this?
Even today there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:25.860
preachers out there - churches who want to&nbsp;
follow Jesus Christ- pure hearts who want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:30.960
to share the Gospel through the Holy Spirit.
But they are struggling to just have food on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:36.240
the table because the church is not willing&nbsp;
to obey God and help them financially.&nbsp;

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:39.480
So I want you to pray about the&nbsp;
church that you're going to.&nbsp;

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:46.020
Ask God - God, am I giving&nbsp;
enough? Or should I give less?

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:51.660
Maybe I should give a little bit less and&nbsp;
maybe give to these people or that people.&nbsp;

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:56.280
You know, you should pray about this&nbsp;
because the Holy Spirit should lead you.&nbsp;

00:18:56.280 --> 00:19:00.660
There are some people who are angry, you&nbsp;
know, when the church talks about this and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:05.160
so a lot of churches don't even preach about this.
They are content with food and clothing and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:09.900
just try to do the best that they can even though&nbsp;
they're struggling to keep bread on the table.&nbsp;

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.200
That's what I saw growing up with my father.&nbsp;

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:19.260
Now on that note, I just want to thank you for&nbsp;
those of you who partnered with me and my team,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:24.960
who are helping us financially to keep on&nbsp;
sharing the Gospel in the way that we do.&nbsp;

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:30.180
We would not have been able&nbsp;
to do this without your help.&nbsp;

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:31.260
So thank you.&nbsp;

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.800
There are some of you that want&nbsp;
to partner with us monthly.&nbsp;

00:19:34.800 --> 00:19:38.040
All the information is in the&nbsp;
video description down below.&nbsp;

00:19:38.580 --> 00:19:43.680
